via `npm run vendor-bergamot`.

NOTE ON LICENSING
The published npm package does not include a LICENSE file and declares no
`license` field in its package.json. Its upstream projects are distributed under
the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (Bergamot / firefox-translations), and the
Marian NMT components it builds on are distributed under the MIT License.

Because the redistributed package states no terms of its own, downstream users
who redistribute this repository — or the built `.plugin` artifact, which embeds
`bergamot-translator-worker.wasm` — should satisfy themselves as to the
applicable terms before doing so. Anyone able to clarify the licensing of the
upstream package is encouraged to open an issue.

Language models are NOT bundled. They are downloaded at runtime from Mozilla's
public model repository and cached locally in the browser's IndexedDB.

